WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Look for circles. What slips away?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Remember what you were looking for.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
In 1999, viewers counted basketball passes.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Some missed an unexpected visitor.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
A classic study of inattentional blindness.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Seeing depends on both eyes and task.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
A goal gives some information priority.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Other details may remain unreported.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
The spotlight is a teaching metaphor.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Missing something does not prove indifference.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
One trial cannot rank your attention.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
A second search is a different condition.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
A busy friend may miss a new haircut.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Ask what held their attention.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Word–color interference is a separate task.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Look again. Leave room for an explanation.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Limited attention calls for clear reminders.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Shift the light. Discover another piece.
